# Dynamic PTCS exact graph alignment

## Pre-work Plan

- Background: RFC-0028 owner graph `Contracts 0.1.29 / Renderer 0.1.76 / Interactive.Client 0.1.67` is publicly released and final SPAA consumer acceptance is green. `DYN-WBS-564` identifies Dynamic.Ptcs, Dynamic.Ptcs.Client and their active tests/live demo as the remaining old exact-package graph.
- Goal: Publish dependency-aligned Dynamic.Ptcs and Dynamic.Ptcs.Client packages and verify active package consumers without changing adapter behavior.
- Assumptions: PTCS `0.2.46` remains the adapter authority; this slice only changes exact package identities/dependencies and evidence.
- Steps: bump package/dependency versions; update active test/live consumers; build and run focused tests/live build; verify local package identity; update WBS/Test/Verification/DevLog; sensitive scan/checker; commit/push; publish/read back only after gates pass.
- Scope: `src/PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Ptcs`, `src/PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Ptcs.Client`, `tests/PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Ptcs.Tests`, `tests/PtcsTaClient.Tests`, `tests/PulseTrade.Comm.Spa.Dynamic.Ptcs.LiveDemo`, and traceability docs. No Renderer/Contracts/runtime behavior changes.
- Acceptance: exact Contracts `[0.1.29]`, Renderer `[0.1.76]`, PTCS `[0.2.46]`; focused tests discovered and pass; LiveDemo Release build passes; nupkg dependencies and versions match; public artifacts are signed and entry-identical after consumer-independent gates.
- Risks: stale direct refs may cause NU1605 downgrade; WebSharper generated-file ACL may require source-identical staging, which must be documented rather than bypassing compiler work.
- Stop condition: adapters are published/read back with active consumers green, or a reproducible external/package blocker prevents further progress.

